  <prompt>
    Add **per-rung telemetry** to the Association Engine and write the **rung 4 + rung 5 unit tests**. Telemetry (DEC-8) measures the deterministic-first ladder on real volume so the team can decide, post-launch, whether to broaden AI-rung usage or adjust the auto-file threshold — you cannot tune what you cannot see. The tests lock the two governing invariants: AI/semantic rungs fire ONLY on deterministic miss/ambiguity, and they NEVER auto-file.

    Telemetry requirements (NFR-05 / DEC-8):
    - Emit per-rung structured telemetry for every association attempt: rung id (0–5), fired vs skipped, latency, match count, resulting confidence + tier (`Resolved`/`Suggested`/`Ambiguous`/`Pending Review`), and for AI rungs (4/5) token/cost + cache hit/miss.
    - Use the telemetry hooks exposed by tasks 030/031; route through the existing BFF telemetry/logging sink (no new telemetry framework — Component Justification §11).
    - Make the deterministic-first invariant observable: a single dashboard-able signal per envelope showing which rung resolved it (or that it fell through to review).

    Test requirements (NFR-08 / ADR-038 KEEP-path):
    - Rung 4 (semantic): fires only when rungs 0–3 miss/are ambiguous; emits `Suggested` (never `Resolved`/auto-file); writes `matchReasons` to provenance; org→`sprk_organization`; consumes the normalized envelope.
    - Rung 5 (AI/JPS): fires only when rungs 0–4 miss/are ambiguous; emits `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` with rationale (never auto-file); privilege flagged not decided (ADR-015); runs via the app-only PublicContracts seam (mocked at the boundary).
    - Ladder integration: a seeded high-confidence deterministic match short-circuits before rung 4/5 fire (assert AI rungs NOT invoked); a deterministic miss escalates to rung 4 then rung 5.
    - Telemetry: assert per-rung records are emitted with the expected fields for both fired + skipped rungs.
    - Follow ADR-038 KEEP-path categories; mock at the boundary (search client, `AppOnlyAnalysisService` PublicContracts seam); no banned patterns.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer + test author; fluent in the Association Engine rung interface, the BFF telemetry/logging sink, `AppOnlyAnalysisService` boundary-mocking, and ADR-038 KEEP-path test classification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Per-rung telemetry emitted for every association attempt (rung id, fired/skipped, latency, match count, tier; tokens/cache for AI rungs), routed through the existing sink. Rung 4 + rung 5 unit tests green, locking the fire-gate (AI fires only on ambiguity/miss) and no-auto-file invariants + provenance/privilege behavior. Ladder short-circuit test proves deterministic high-confidence matches never invoke AI rungs. Build + tests green; publish-size delta + CVE reported; `/conflict-check` clean.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      NFR-05 mandates a deterministic-first ladder with AI rungs firing only on ambiguity/miss; DEC-8 requires real-volume measurement before broadening AI usage or moving the auto-file threshold. Rung 4 (task 030) + rung 5 (task 031) exposed telemetry hooks; this task consumes them and adds the tests that lock the invariants. The auto-file boundary (FR-11 owner override) is the highest-value thing to test: deterministic ≥0.85 auto-files; AI rungs never do.
    </background>
