  <steps>
    <step order="1">Run `/conflict-check` (BFF hot-path). Load `bff-extensions.md`. Read the rung 4/5 telemetry hooks (tasks 030/031) + the existing BFF telemetry/logging sink to confirm the emission surface.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement per-rung telemetry emission in the engine: for each rung attempt emit rung id, fired/skipped, latency, match count, resulting confidence + tier; for rungs 4/5 add tokens/cost + cache hit/miss. Route through the existing sink. Add a single per-envelope "resolving rung" signal.</step>
    <step order="3">Author rung 4 unit tests (fire-gate on deterministic miss; `Suggested`-only; `matchReasons` provenance; org→`sprk_organization`; envelope-only input) — mock the search client at the boundary.</step>
    <step order="4">Author rung 5 unit tests (fire-gate on rung-0–4 miss; `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` with rationale; never auto-file; privilege flagged not decided; app-only via mocked PublicContracts seam).</step>
    <step order="5">Author ladder-integration tests: (a) seeded deterministic ≥0.85 → `Resolved`/auto-file AND rung 4/5 NOT invoked; (b) deterministic miss → rung 4 fires → rung 5 fires; (c) conflicting high-confidence → `Ambiguous`.</step>
    <step order="6">Author telemetry tests: assert per-rung records emitted with expected fields for both fired + skipped rungs (via a fake/spy sink).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (clean) + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication` (all green).</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — no new HIGH CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">TEST-MODIFYING quality gates (UNCONDITIONAL per root §8): invoke `code-review` on telemetry code + tests; invoke `adr-check` against ADR-038, ADR-015, ADR-024 + `spec.md`. Address Critical + High findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: mark 032 ✅; W3 complete.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `current-task.md` per task-execute protocol: status → completed; advance to next pending task.</step>
  </steps>

