  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-rung telemetry emitted for every attempt: rung id, fired/skipped, latency, match count, tier; rungs 4/5 also emit tokens/cost + cache hit/miss.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A per-envelope "resolving rung" signal is emitted (dashboard-able).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rung 4 tests: fires only on deterministic miss; `Suggested`-only; `matchReasons` in provenance; org→`sprk_organization`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Rung 5 tests: fires only on rung-0–4 miss; `Suggested`/`Ambiguous` with rationale; never auto-files; privilege flagged not decided.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Ladder test: deterministic ≥0.85 short-circuits — rung 4/5 NOT invoked; deterministic miss escalates 4→5.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Telemetry tests assert expected per-rung fields for fired + skipped rungs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tests use boundary mocks (search client, PublicContracts seam); no ADR-038 banned patterns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build + Communication tests green; publish-size delta + CVE reported; `/conflict-check` clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Telemetry is the DEC-8 measurement substrate — the post-launch decision to broaden AI-rung usage or move the auto-file threshold depends on it. Keep the emission cheap (structured log/metric fields, not a new pipeline). Tests are MAINTAIN-class (invariant contracts) and survive the `/test-diet` gate. The AI-never-auto-file and deterministic-short-circuit assertions are the load-bearing ones — do not let them regress.
  </notes>

  <completion>
    Central per-rung telemetry added to `IncomingAssociationResolver` (existing `ILogger` sink — §11, no new
    pipeline): `EvaluateRungsAsync` emits one structured record per rung attempt (`EventId 4501` —
    CommunicationId, Rung, RungOrder, IsAiRung, Outcome fired/skipped/error, MatchCount, ElapsedMs via
    Stopwatch.GetTimestamp/GetElapsedTime); `ResolveAsync` emits one per-envelope resolving-rung summary
    (`EventId 4502` — Tier, AutoFiled, ResolvingRungs [rungs contributing to written targets], RungsFired),
    derived from already-computed provenance. **Tokens/cost + cache hit/miss for AI rungs (4/5) = documented
    follow-up** — the facades (IRecordMatchingAi / ICommunicationClassificationAi / IOpenAiClient) don't
    surface usage to the caller; plumbing them changes the PublicContracts seam (blast radius, out of scope).
    IsAiRung flag emitted so a dashboard can partition deterministic vs AI cost today.

    22 new tests (boundary mocks only, ADR-038 KEEP-path, 0 banned patterns): SemanticMatchRungTests (9),
    AiClassificationRungTests (6), AssociationLadderIntegrationTests (3), RungTelemetryTests (4) + shared
    RungTestSupport (CapturingLogger spy + FakeRung + scope-factory/search builders). Load-bearing invariants
    locked: deterministic ≥0.85 short-circuits (AI facades Times.Never); AI rungs never bear a target /
    never auto-file; conflict→Ambiguous; privilege = signal-only (ADR-015).

    Build clean; 324 Communication tests green (22 new, 0 fail, 5 pre-existing skips); publish 45.30 MB
    compressed incl-PDBs (+0.02 delta, ≤60 ceiling); CVE = pre-existing Kiota 1.21.2 High only (0 new);
    /conflict-check clean; Step 9.5 gates (code-review + adr-check) 0 Critical / 0 ADR violations. W3 COMPLETE.
  </completion>

